# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Fei Shuang et al. (2026). Model accuracy and data heterogeneity shape uncertainty quantification in machine learning interatomic potentials.
#   Machine Learning Science and Technology. doi:10.1088/2632-2153/ae3d80  arXiv:2508.03405v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2508.03405v1 (sha256 810505f182b9b4d9...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 350 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/shuang2026accuracy.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: six-member ensembles of linear ACE models for BCC
# tungsten (pacemaker; 15 to 945 basis functions; kappa = 0.01, at most
# 2,000 steps) trained on subsets A+B of the authors' earlier W data set,
# with the energy and force RMSEs stated for Func-15 and Func-945 in the
# Fig. 2 caption. The other models (4 of the 6 sizes), the A+D training
# combination and all uncertainty-error correlations, thresholds and
# selection rates are figure-only or UQ diagnostics.

